  "final_proposal": {
    "title": "The Slow Lane",
    "idea": "Mastercard built its name on making payment faster. Now it says: not everything should be. With partner grocers, pharmacies and markets, one checkout lane is set aside as unhurried, marked 'This lane takes its time.' It is open to anyone, so nobody has to say they are lonely. Cashiers opt in, are given the time to talk, and are recognised for it. An optional 'Slow Tap' swaps the efficient beep for a warmer pause, using Mastercard's sonic identity. It starts as a measured, off-peak pilot with a loneliness charity as advisor, and results are published. If it works, it grows into Slow Hour and Slow Day. The checkout, often the only conversation someone has all day, becomes a place to be known.",
