    "title": "Overdue",
    "idea": "Most people aren't short of friends. They're stuck on the awkward first message after too long. Overdue turns the most dreaded piece of financial mail into an invitation. Cardholders opt in and list people they owe a catch-up. Their bank app sends a mock notice: 'Amount due: one coffee, one catch-up. Overdue by 14 months.' When both people pay with their own Mastercard at the same local venue, the first round is partly refunded. Only a payments brand can own this language, and the value is the reunion, not the spend. Safeguards keep it kind: snooze or forgive any debt, settle with a call or walk, and donate the rebate to a loneliness charity. It grows through 'paid in full' stories, an annual Overdue Day, and workplace and city editions.",
