  "final_proposal": {
    "title": "Owe Me One",
    "idea": "Every bill split and covered coffee creates a small debt, and that debt is usually a reason to see someone again. Owe Me One adds a new option to peer-to-peer payments: 'Settle in person'. Instead of sending money, the payer says 'I'll get you back', and the app sets a shared date. A payments brand choosing not to complete a transaction is the provocation: time with people is the one currency that can't be sent digitally. A pilot with a P2P partner and partner cafes would host the meetups, with a graceful fallback to a normal payment if plans slip. Social and content ask one question: 'Who do you owe one?' Success is measured in meetups that actually happen.",
