    "title": "The Extra Inch",
    "idea": "Inside a well-made Dior couture garment, a hidden inch of seam allowance lets it be taken in, let out and refitted for decades. The campaign reveals that inch as the house's quiet promise of a long life. The inch becomes a film motif, a unit of measure and the name of a service: book a refit, adjust a piece as life changes, or prepare it to be passed on. Real owners and atelier hands tell the stories. For bags and shoes, resoling, re-edging and re-strapping become 'the next inch'. A published Extra Inch Standard and stated atelier capacity make the promise verifiable. Luxury becomes a long relationship with a garment, not a single purchase.",
