      "reason": "This keeps C2's social value and credibility without letting the campaign read as CSR or become patronising."
    }
  ],
  "final_proposal": {
    "title": "Take Your Time",
    "idea": "Contactless made paying instant, and for many people it quietly removed the last small conversation of their day. Take Your Time gives some of it back. Independent cafes, markets and corner shops display a simple Mastercard counter mark that means 'I've got a minute.' A customer who wants to join just pauses before tapping, and the merchant answers with a chat. A softer, unhurried version of the Mastercard sound marks the moment. Nobody has to say they're lonely, and anyone can take part. Mastercard openly admits the cost of speed and turns Priceless into the smallest, most human form of itself: a minute of someone's time. It launches with committed local merchants in quiet-hour windows, then grows through signage, sound, PR and social.",
